# Junk files from shell commands with unescaped quote/backtick characters
`
'
# Zero-byte artifacts left when an external tool echoes edited/command content
# through a shell and a '>' in the content is taken as a redirect (the token
# after it becomes an empty file). Only shell-metacharacter names are matched —
# they never occur in real source here; identifier-like stragglers can't be
# pattern-matched safely, so stage changes explicitly rather than `git add -A`.
